          "en": "turn this into a shell script.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.87,
          "end": 17.57,
          "en": "Best practice for shell scripts is to use bash most of the time, so probably arrays.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.57,
          "end": 20.57,
          "en": "We will not use that much in an interactive environment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.6,
          "end": 25.37,
          "en": "Nonetheless, I want to have this lecture here to just visualize the problems that happen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.37,
          "end": 28.69,
          "en": "If we are not aware of which shall we are using right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.7,
          "end": 33.77,
          "en": "So let's say we got an array fruits and they contain apple, banana and passion fruit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 33.8,
          "end": 37.04,
          "en": "Then we could try to access the element with the index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 37.04,
          "end": 37.55,
          "en": "One.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.55,
          "end": 38.96,
          "en": "What will be printed here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.96,
          "end": 43.01,
          "en": "Well in bash it will print out banana because we start counting at zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.04,
          "end": 48.35,
          "en": "This to me personally actually feels quite intuitive because I feel like in programming languages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.35,
          "end": 51.98,
          "en": "I'm just used to arrays to start counting at zero.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.98,
          "end": 54.2,
          "en": "So here in this case, banana will be printed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.2,
          "end": 57.59,
          "en": "Let's just confirm here I'm in Bash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.04,
          "end": 61.98,
          "en": "It's configured right now that the bash is using the dollar symbol here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.46,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "So here, let me just create my fruits, apple, banana and passion fruit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 71.37,
          "end": 76.47,
          "en": "And then I just want to output one of those fruits, fruits, square bracket one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.47,
          "end": 81.33,
          "en": "And then we can see here, this is now printing out the banana.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 81.57,
          "end": 82.74,
          "en": "All looks good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 82.95,
          "end": 89.76,
          "en": "However, in zsh it will print out apple because by default, yes, there are ways to change this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 89.76,
          "end": 95.61,
          "en": "but by default it will print out apple because the array indexing starts at one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "This means if I would take exactly the same thing here and I would just use this over here somehow,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 104.64,
          "en": "copy and paste with the keyboard doesn't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 104.67,
          "end": 106.25999999999999,
          "en": "It added additional characters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 106.25999999999999,
          "end": 107.81,
          "en": "Oh, well, um.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 108.18,
          "end": 110.82,
          "en": "So here we are, exactly the same code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.82,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "This also defines an array and that is H, which is already great.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 116.19,
          "en": "They share the same syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 116.19,
          "end": 122.46,
          "en": "But if we have a look here, if I try to access the first element here, we can see we are getting apple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 123.51,
          "en": "and not banana.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.53,
          "end": 131.13,
          "en": "This is the reason is again in bash array indexes start at zero and that as H they start at one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 131.79,
          "end": 133.92,
          "en": "As you can see, this is a little bit different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 133.92,
          "end": 139.18,
          "en": "And then also how we get the number of elements, what syntax styles are supported.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.2,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "There is also slightly different in, for example, in Zsh we could get the number of elements slightly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "shorter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.93,
          "en": "We could just do it like this and get the number of elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 151.44,
          "end": 153.48,
          "en": "In bash we need to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.51,
          "end": 159.75,
          "en": "We can't do this because this will count the number of letters of the first element and to get the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.75,
